<title>UK: Commercial Union up amid vague bid talk.</title>
<headline>Commercial Union up amid vague bid talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Commercial Union Plc gained on Monday, defying weakness elsewhere in the UK stock market as vague bid rumours returned around the insurance stock, dealers said.</p>
<p>The stock was up 16p at 699-1/2 by 1401 GMT in volume of 1.6 million shares, even as the FTSE 100 index traded down 70.4 points at 4,806.8.</p>
<p>&quot;It is a strange move with the FTSE down 70 points but volume is quite thin,&quot; said one dealer, &quot;people have linked it with ABN AMRO but maybe it is just a bit of switching in the sector.&quot;</p>
<p>Commercial Union said its policy was to not comment on market speculation.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
